# Every text file is checked out with CRLF, whatever the machine's core.autocrlf says.
#
# The release archive packs source files, and the settings window compiles in a manifest,
# so their line endings are part of the release's bytes. With the checkout left to each
# machine's Git configuration, two builds of the same tag produced different archives
# depending on who cloned it - which made "build it yourself and compare the digest" a
# test of someone's Git settings rather than of the release. The repository stores LF;
# only the working tree is fixed. Binary files are detected and left alone.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Windows launchers must keep CRLF wherever they are unpacked, including a
# release ZIP downloaded on another platform.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.txt text eol=crlf
